<section class="neuron-models" aria-labelledby="neuron-models-title">
  <p class="section-label">Neuron models</p>
  <div>
    <h2 id="neuron-models-title">Two cell types, two model representations</h2>
    <div class="cell-models">
      <figure>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 260 112" role="img" aria-labelledby="pyramidal-diagram-title">
          <title id="pyramidal-diagram-title">Pyramidal neuron modeled as coupled soma and dendrite compartments</title>
          <line x1="106" y1="46" x2="154" y2="46" />
          <circle cx="76" cy="46" r="30" />
          <circle cx="184" cy="46" r="30" />
          <text x="76" y="51" class="voltage">V<tspan baseline-shift="sub" font-size="11">s</tspan></text>
          <text x="184" y="51" class="voltage">V<tspan baseline-shift="sub" font-size="11">d</tspan></text>
          <text x="76" y="100">Soma</text>
          <text x="184" y="100">Dendrite</text>
        </svg>
        <figcaption>
          <h3>Pyramidal neurons</h3>
          <p class="model-name">Bursting Pinsky–Rinzel model</p>
          <p>Two coupled compartments represent the soma and dendrite, capturing the bursting activity of excitatory pyramidal cells.</p>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 260 112" role="img" aria-labelledby="interneuron-diagram-title">
          <title id="interneuron-diagram-title">PV interneuron modeled as a single membrane-voltage compartment</title>
          <circle cx="130" cy="46" r="30" />
          <text x="130" y="51" class="voltage">V</text>
          <text x="130" y="100">Single compartment</text>
        </svg>
        <figcaption>
          <h3>PV interneurons</h3>
          <p class="model-name">Wang–Buzsáki model</p>
          <p>A single compartment represents fast-spiking parvalbumin (PV) interneurons, which provide inhibition and help synchronize network activity.</p>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
